        <body>
            <div xml:id="d496">

                <pb facs="0571" n="511" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg511"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr.
                            Runyon</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-02-06"><hi rendition="#italic">February 6,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 224.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch, No. 185, of the 5th ultimo,
                    relative to the apprehended danger to trade between the United States and
                    Germany, if the grounds of complaint of the latter as to the special duty on
                    sugar be not removed, has been received and read with attention.</p>
                <p>You have doubtless learned from the public press that the sugar differential
                    repeal bill has passed the House of Representatives.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
